# Build context filter for packaging/synology/Dockerfile. BuildKit reads it instead of a root
# .dockerignore because it sits next to the Dockerfile with a matching name.
#
# Allow list: only the sources the staged projects are built from enter the context. Later
# lines win, so the exclusions below also apply inside the allowed directories.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!web/
!LICENSE
!packaging/synology/

# Output of build.ps1 / build.sh (staged projects, SPKs); it must never feed the next build
packaging/synology/dist

# Version control and local tooling state
.git
.claude

# Local environment files may hold secrets and must never reach a build layer
**/.env*
**/*.local

# Dependencies and build output; the web stage installs and builds its own
**/node_modules
bin
**/*.exe
**/*.test
internal/adapters/http/webui/dist
web/**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Coverage and Playwright output
**/coverage
**/coverage.out
**/coverage.html
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report
